<title>ITALY: Italy's Finmeccanica MD resigns.</title>
<headline>Italy's Finmeccanica MD resigns.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian engineering group Finmeccanica said on Thursday Bruno Steve had stepped down as managing director.</p>
<p>&quot;Bruno Steve has resigned as chief executive of Finmeccanica, considering his task complete after seeing the company through a delicate phase,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Finmeccanica, which is contolled by state holding Iri, earlier this month signed a joint venture with Britain's General Electric Co Plc to take minority stakes in some of their respective defence operations.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
